"""What the national street trees do through the year, for the species CW_TREE_SEASON (index.html) does not cover.

Same fields as CW_TREE_SEASON -- p: wind-pollen months, b: [from, to, what] bloom, f: [from, to, color] fall color,
months as decimals (10.5 = mid-Oct) -- plus t: one line in words, with regional timing where it matters, and
ev: true for an evergreen (nothing to say about fall color; the page can say EVERGREEN).

HOME: each entry is written in the calendar of the place it is a common street tree (None = New York, the
calendar CW_TREE_SEASON uses). season.py turns every entry into New York's calendar by subtracting the home city's
shift (shifts.py), so the page does ONE thing for every species: NYC time + the city's shift.
"""
